{"text": "PHILIP MORRIS U. S.A.\nINTER-OFFICE CORRESPONDENCE\nRichmond, Virginia\n\nTo oo: BAL = - Date: March 28, 1991\nFron: G. M. Bankl\n\nSubject: Sludge Sample Request From Park 500.\n\nAs you know, sludge analyses in addition to those being provided by R&D are\nnecessary to properly evaluate the feasibility of co-firing at Park 500.\nGabriel Laboratories of Chicago has been contracted to perform this\nadditional work which is intended to determine the potential of the sludge\nas a supplemental fuel stuff, and to aid in predicting the impact of co-\nfiring on the boiler. The following analyses will be performed by Gabriel:\nProximate Analysis, Ultimate Analysis, Ash Fusion Analysis. Ash Mineral\nanalysis.\n\nSamples of process centrifuge sludge and waste treatment sludge under the\nconditions of ferric chloride treatment for phosphorus removal will be\nrequired for the above analytical work. All samples are to be composite\nsamples collected over at least a 24 hour period. Four quart jars packed to\nzero headspace are to be provided for each of the two sludges. The samples\nshould be collected using a stainless steel scoop which has been detergent\nwashed and rinsed with deionized water between each sampling. The samples\nshould algo be homogenized prior to packing in the quart jars.\n\nThe eight sample jars along with a shipping cooler and refrigerated packing\nwill be supplied by Gabriel. No preservatives are necessary other than\nrefrigeration. The jars will be prelabeled indicating the sludge tyre and\ndescription. The sampler will complete the remainder of the label ( i.e.,\nsample date, tine, sampler, etc. ) as well as complete the provided chain of\ncustody form. An example of a sample label and chain of custody form has\nbeen attached for your review.\n\nAll of the above items will be delivered to Park 500 sometime during the week\nof April 1, and have been addressed to the attention of John Petchul. The\nfull cample jars and completed forns must be returned to Gabriel via Federal\nExpress or U.P.S., and should be addressed to the attention of Ms. Mary Shuey.\nSaipping charges may be billed to Engineering using the change nusber\n44-078.\n\nIn order to stay on track with the current project schedule, all samples\nmust be delivered to Gabriel by May 6. A full month turn around is expected\nbefore the results will be available. A meeting has been scheduled for 10:30\nam at Park 500 on April 5 during which additional discussion regarding this\nrequest and the project schedule will take place.\n\ncc: W. S. Apple J. J. Petohul\nG.L. Hill J. M. Waitman\nJ. EL Narron\n\n2030490773", "words": [{"text": "PHILIP", "x0": 328, "y0": 141, "x1": 369, "y1": 151, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "MORRIS", "x0": 376, "y0": 142, "x1": 417, "y1": 152, "conf": 88.0}, {"text": "U.", "x0": 424, "y0": 142, "x1": 436, "y1": 152, "conf": 88.0}, {"text": "S.A.", "x0": 445, "y0": 142, "x1": 478, "y1": 152, "conf": 41.0}, {"text": "INTER-OFFICE", "x0": 221, "y0": 162, "x1": 383, "y1": 173, "conf": 16.0}, {"text": "CORRESPONDENCE", "x0": 403, "y0": 163, "x1": 592, "y1": 174, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "Richmond,", "x0": 341, "y0": 184, "x1": 401, "y1": 196, "conf": 56.0}, {"text": "Virginia", "x0": 410, "y0": 185, "x1": 465, "y1": 196, "conf": 0.0}, {"text": "To", "x0": 128, "y0": 240, "x1": 142, "y1": 250, "conf": 83.0}, {"text": "oo:", "x0": 179, "y0": 243, "x1": 182, "y1": 245, "conf": 47.0}, {"text": "BAL", "x0": 198, "y0": 240, "x1": 231, "y1": 250, "conf": 57.0}, {"text": "=", "x0": 241, "y0": 241, "x1": 289, "y1": 279, "conf": 64.0}, {"text": "-", "x0": 341, "y0": 244, "x1": 344, "y1": 246, "conf": 46.0}, {"text": "Date:", "x0": 458, "y0": 242, "x1": 491, "y1": 252, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "March", "x0": 507, "y0": 242, "x1": 542, "y1": 252, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "28,", "x0": 549, "y0": 242, "x1": 568, "y1": 253, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "1991", "x0": 578, "y0": 243, "x1": 604, "y1": 252, "conf": 91.0}, {"text": "Fron:", "x0": 129, "y0": 268, "x1